# def.domain-discovery

domain discovery = exhume the objects, operations, and language that already exist in the domain, so code speaks the domain's own words. discover, never invent: the truth is buried under mechanism, jargon, and tool shape; dig it out intact
ground truth = the real-world practice and the people who do the work. a schema, an api response, a legacy class name is only a description of it, lossy and incidental
> the map is not the territory. the schema is not the domain.
the surf instructor says "a surfer books a lesson" → `SurfLesson`, never `Reservation` (a table kept it that way). code and expert disagree → the expert is right
surface → beneath: a record's shape → the object the domain has · the last tool's jargon → the expert's word · how a step runs → why it exists · a borrowed synonym → the one canonical term
a term that names the surface decays with it; a term that names the buried truth outlives every rewrite. name the motive; motives outlast mechanisms
the test — discovered, not invented: an expert recognizes it with no gloss · it names what is or why, never how · one sense in the domain · it composes (objects nest, operations chain). cannot point to where it lived in the domain → you invented it; dig deeper
caveat: exhume what the domain holds today; a truth not yet found is a note on record, not a mandate to build (rule.prefer.wet-over-dry)
see also: howto.domain-discovery · ref.domain-discovery.fundamentals · rule.require.ubiqlang (mechanic) · philosophy.domain-as-a-garden
